<title>FRANCE: France may accept EMU pact before parliament meets.</title>
<headline>France may accept EMU pact before parliament meets.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch Prime Minister Wim Kok said on Tuesday that France's new Socialist-led government had told him it could accept a pact limiting budget deficits of countries that join a single European currency before it presents its policies to parliament on June 19.</p>
<p>&quot;The French government told us they do not have to wait for the presentation before the National Assembly,&quot; Kok told a news conference after talks with new Socialist Prime Minister Lionel Jospin.</p>
</text>
